## Your answer

Return a single JSON object matching the required schema. No prose before or
after it, and no markdown code fence.

Rules for specific fields:

- `primary_issue` — the main problem, in one short phrase.
- `secondary_issue` — only when a genuinely separate second problem exists.
- `entities` — only identifiers actually present in the complaint text. Do not
  infer an order number that was not written.
- `policy_refs` — only extracts shown above, with `chunk_key` copied exactly.
- `resolution_steps` — concrete actions an agent can take. Steps that depend on
  verification must say so ("verify X, then...").
- `escalation_required` / `escalation_level` — your assessment, which the rule
  engine will check. If true, `escalation_level` is required.
- `missing_information` — what you needed and did not have.
- `clarification_questions` — required when `insufficient_information` is true.
  Ask for the missing fact; never invent it.
- `summary` — two or three sentences for the agent, not for the customer.
- `agent_guidance` — internal notes. Use kind CAUTION for anything the agent
  must avoid doing.
